  "review": "2026-11-06: reviewed merged source against f32941b and fcc277e. Restored Android-only pairing API, foreground-service lifecycle, binding gate, MAC normalization and local crash diagnostics; no Harmony equivalent claimed. Ledger/current-driving/AT behavior retained from 0.6.0; both firmware resources are 4.1.2 with GNSS and independent mileage. Raw-file newline changes reviewed as non-semantic. Host tests recorded in docs/RELEASE_4_6_2.md; no new HAP/device validation. 2026-11-09: reviewed final 4.1.2 manifest provenance fields; application sources unchanged. Harmony 0.6.1 adds matching 4.0.6/4.0.7 rollback packages and correct application version labels.",
  "sourceReview20261109": {
    "scope": "Unreleased source changes only; not a visual or device acceptance result",
    "reviewed": [
      "MainActivity settings rows: 7dp padding produces a 24dp glyph in the existing 38dp tile, matching Harmony",
      "SettingsIconView: respects explicit padding; unpadded navigation and other callers retain their viewport",
      "TransferMerge: both platforms categorize conflicts, count refuel generations once and compare registration values independent of JSON key order",
      "TransferArchive/Schema/Store/DataTransferActivity: v7 exports explicit bookkeeping mode, reads v1-v6; matching Harmony archive/schema/repository and visible upgrade notice; old archives preserve local mode"
    ],
    "deviceValidation": "Deferred by user; full UI/behavior parity not certified"
  },
  "sourceReview20261110": {
    "scope": "Startup preference and Android-only independent waiting notification channel; not device acceptance",
    "reviewed": [
      "Android saved-instance state and notification intents take precedence over the configured startup page; Harmony notification intent also takes precedence",
      "Default startup page is portable via v7 int preference on both platforms",
      "Waiting-only Android notification channel is user-controlled through system settings; active connection/OTA and low fuel retain existing channels",
      "Harmony has no equivalent permanent waiting notification to hide; no background-running policy change"
    ]
  },
  "sourceReview20261112": {
    "scope": "Release 4.6.4 gauge boot defaults; source/protocol review only, device validation deferred",
    "reviewed": [
      "Removed App launch-tab selection in Android and Harmony; saved-instance/notification navigation remains intact",
      "Both gauge settings pages expose the same nine boot pages and clockwise 0/90/180/270-degree orientation, only with a valid v3 snapshot",
      "Both clients serialize writes and verify actual gauge readback; defaults apply on next gauge power-on; Android keeps requests for different setting kinds independently",
      "Legacy v4.6.3 default_start_tab remains an ignored archive key so released v7 backups remain importable; other portable preferences retained",
      "Independent Android waiting notification channel remains unchanged"
    ]
  }
